## 3. VFX Supervisor QA & Technical Audit

**Verdict:** [Approved for Concept / Rejected for Direct Comp / Requires Nuke fixes]

1. Mechanical Interaction & Tool Physics (Critical Fail)
Lack of Torque & Dynamic Recoil: A high-torque  3/4 impact wrench driving or loosening lug nuts on heavy plant machinery produces aggressive axial vibration, hammer impact stutter, and wrist counter-torque. The tool and the operator’s arms remain unnaturally static, floating against the lug without dynamic mechanical bite.

Socket-to-Nut Registration: As the camera pushes in (00:01–00:03), the socket barrel does not maintain rigid concentric alignment with the nut. Instead of hard-surface rotational friction or lock, the contact point exhibits subtle drifting/sliding across the stud face.

Tool Geometry Warping: The battery pack base and motor housing exhibit micro-morphing across the push. The trigger finger and trigger guard lack defined mechanical clearance.

2. Hard-Surface Coherence & Typography (High Priority)
Tire Sidewall Text: The raised sidewall branding displays classic generative gibberish typography (pseudo-lettering resembling “...GLOBA OM...”) that subtly changes depth and relief as the camera perspective shifts.

Rim & Stud Symmetry:

The bolt-circle pitch and spacing become irregular along the lower quadrant of the hub.

Several perimeter nuts/studs lose hexagonal definition and melt into rounded, ambiguous metal plugs between 00:02 and 00:04.

The center grease/hub cap perimeter lacks clean circular concentricity with the wheel rim bore.

3. Anatomical & Material Coherence (Medium Priority)
Support Hand (Left Glove): The left hand stabilizing the front housing of the impact wrench shows geometric swimming. The thumb and index finger blend together around the neck of the tool at 00:02, lacking distinct knuckle articulation and compressive contact with the rubberized tool grip.

Texture Boiling (Temporal Crawl): Dirt and grease spatters on the work pants and hi-vis vest do not remain completely pinned to the underlying fabric folds, exhibiting minor temporal noise (sub-pixel crawling) typical of diffusion temporal layers.

4. Optical & Edge Integration
Bokeh Falloff & Alpha Bleed: The edge matte separation between the worker's hard hat/vest and the excavator in the out-of-focus background shows soft edge smearing. The depth map appears slightly dilated, pulling pieces of the background blur into the high-frequency edges of the jacket.

Rigid-Body Parallax: While large-scale camera parallax is relatively stable, the wheel face does not hold up as a true rigid 3D plane; the perspective distortion on the rim rim lip breathes slightly during the move.

VFX Supervisor Verdict & Comp Fixability
Status: REJECTED FOR HERO/FOREGROUND FINAL (Usable only as deep background plate element or under heavy motion blur / brief cutaways < 12 frames).

Comp / 2D Patch Viability:

Low/Cost-Inefficient: Fixing the socket contact, rebuilding the bolt circle, replacing the sidewall typography, and stabilizing the hand deformation would require extensive 3D projection tracking, a CG wheel replacement, and clean-plate hand paintouts.

If this asset must be delivered, recommend tracking and projecting a clean CAD/photogrammetry wheel rim and replacement impact wrench onto the tracked plate, using the live footage primarily for the worker's core body mass.
